menu "Doorbell firmware"

    config DOORBELL_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "GPIO of the doorbell push button"
        range 0 7 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
        default 0
        help
            GPIO connected to the doorbell contact. Must be an LP/RTC capable
            pin, because it is the deep-sleep wake-up source (GPIO0..GPIO7 on
            the ESP32-C6). The contact is wired against GND, the internal
            pull-up is enabled.

    config DOORBELL_ED_TIMEOUT
        int "End device timeout (index)"
        range 0 14
        default 6
        help
            0=10s 1=2min 2=4min 3=8min 4=16min 5=32min 6=64min 7=128min ...
            Tells the parent how long it keeps the child record before it
            considers this device gone (ezb_nwk_ed_timeout_e).

    config DOORBELL_KEEPALIVE_MS
        int "Poll interval while awake (ms)"
        default 1000
        help
            Poll interval used while the device is awake (interview window,
            button reporting). The device sleeps in deep sleep afterwards, so
            this only affects the few awake seconds.

    config DOORBELL_JOIN_AWAKE_S
        int "Stay awake after a fresh join (s)"
        default 120
        help
            After joining a network for the first time the device stays awake
            for this long, polling fast, so the coordinator can complete the
            interview. Without it the device would sleep in the middle of the
            interview.

    config DOORBELL_KEEPALIVE_WAKE_S
        int "Periodic keepalive wake-up (s, 0 = off)"
        default 0
        help
            Deep sleep loses the parent link after DOORBELL_ED_TIMEOUT. With a
            periodic wake-up the device re-attaches regularly and stays
            "online" in the coordinator. Each wake-up costs roughly 6 mAh/1000,
            so 0 (only wake on button press) is the lowest power setting; the
            first press after a long idle then needs an extra rejoin.

    config DOORBELL_GPIO_PROBE
        bool "Log the level of GPIO0..GPIO10 while awake (pin identification)"
        default n
        help
            Prints the level of the LP-capable GPIOs every 500 ms so the pin a
            button is actually wired to can be found. Use together with a long
            DOORBELL_BOOT_AWAKE_S.

    config DOORBELL_BOOT_AWAKE_S
        int "Stay awake after power-on (s)"
        default 10
        help
            Deep sleep powers down the USB PHY, so the board disappears from
            /dev/ttyACM* while sleeping. After a power-on reset (hub power
            cycle, EN reset) the firmware therefore stays awake for this long
            before the first deep sleep, which is the window used to flash or
            to watch the serial console.

    config DOORBELL_SELFTEST
        bool "Inject a virtual button press after boot (bench test)"
        default n
        help
            Treats every boot as a button press. Only for bring-up tests.

    config DOORBELL_SELFTEST_REBOOT_S
        int "Self-test: sleep period between simulated presses (s)"
        depends on DOORBELL_SELFTEST
        default 20
        help
            In self-test mode every boot counts as one press and the normal
            deep-sleep path is taken, with this period as the timer wake-up, so
            a press cycle repeats by itself without touching the hardware.

endmenu
